# Capstone Project — Cursor Rules

## Stack

- **Runtime:** Node.js (LTS, v18+)
- **Package manager:** npm
- **Language:** JavaScript (CommonJS or ES modules as configured in package.json)

## Conventions

- **Commits:** Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format (e.g. `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`).
- **Indentation:** 2 spaces — no tabs.
- **Dependencies:** Ask before adding new npm packages. Prefer built-in Node.js APIs and existing dependencies when possible.

## General

- Keep changes focused and minimal.
- Match existing file structure and naming patterns.
- Do not commit secrets or `.env` files.

## Lessons from FE-05 workflow drill

- All form inputs must have an associated <label>, aria-invalid state, and aria-describedby linking to the error message
- Any new form/validation logic requires accompanying test files (validator + storage/persistence layers), run via npm test before considering the task done
- Validation rules must explicitly reject edge cases (leading/trailing whitespace, consecutive dots, disallowed characters) — "looks valid" is not the same as tested valid